wers are: My hand currently has 3 tiles: T3, B7, B7, F1, F1. I have three melds: a pung of T1 (exposed via Peng), a kong of W3 (exposed via Gang), and a chow of T4 T5 T6 (exposed via Chi T5). I need one more meld and a pair to complete a standard hand (4 melds + pair). My hand tiles are T3, B7, B7, F1, F1. I have a pair of F1 and a pair of B7, and a single T3. To win, I need to either complete the T3 into a meld (e.g., get T2 and T4 for a chow, or get two more T3 for a pung) or change my hand structure. The unseen tile counts show T3 has 2 left, B7 has 3 left, F1 has 3 left. Discarding T3 leaves me with two pairs (B7 and F1), which is a standard two-pair wait for a winning tile to complete a pung for either pair, or to draw the other B7/F1 to make a kong and then need another pair. Discarding B7 leaves me with T3 and two F1; I'd need to complete T3 into a meld and use F1 as pair, or get another F1 for a pung and find a pair elsewhere. Discarding F1 leaves me with T3 and two B7; similar situation. Considering scoring potential: I have an exposed kong of W3, exposed pung of T1, and exposed chow of T4-T6. My hand has terminals/honors: T1, T3, T4, T5, T6, W3, B7, F1. Possible patterns: All Pungs (if I get another pung), Half Flush (since my suits are mainly T with one W3 and B7, but W3 is a kong, so not all same suit), maybe All Types (I have W, T, B, and F1 honor, but need a dragon? Actually dragons are J, I don't have any, so not All Types). I have a pung of T1 which is terminal, so Pung of Terminals or Honors (1 point). I have a kong of W3 which is simple, no extra. My pair of F1 is East Wind, which is Prevailing Wind (East), so if I win with F1 pair, I get Seat Wind? Seat Wind is West (F3), not F1. So F1 is only Prevailing Wind, not Seat Wind. So if I win with F1 pair, I get Prevalent Wind (2 points). But I need at least 8 points total to win. Currently, I have: from melds: Pung of Terminals or Honors (T1) = 1 point. Kong of W3 (simple) = 0. Chow of T4-T6 (simple) =